{"tool_name":"flimma","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"flimma","home":"https://exbio.wzw.tum.de/flimma/","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Flimma is a federated privacy-aware version of state-of-the art differential expression analysis method limma voom.","addition_date":"2022-06-07T16:25:38.553368Z","last_update_date":"2022-06-07T16:25:38.556008Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:flimma","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"olya.zolotareva@gmail.com","name":"Olga Zolotareva","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9424-8052","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Julian Matschinske"},{"name":"Reihaneh Torkzadehmahani"},{"name":"Reza Nasirigerdeh"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Differential gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene expression QTL analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3232"}]}],"name":"Flimma","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02553-2","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Aggregating transcriptomics data across hospitals can increase sensitivity and robustness of differential expression analyses, yielding deeper clinical insights. As data exchange is often restricted by privacy legislation, meta-analyses are frequently employed to pool local results. However, the accuracy might drop if class labels are inhomogeneously distributed among cohorts. Flimma (https://exbio.wzw.tum.de/flimma/) addresses this issue by implementing the state-of-the-art workflow limma voom in a federated manner, i.e., patient data never leaves its source site. Flimma results are identical to those generated by limma voom on aggregated datasets even in imbalanced scenarios where meta-analysis approaches fail.","authors":[{"name":"Abbasinejad A."},{"name":"Bakhtiari M."},{"name":"Baumbach J."},{"name":"Blumenthal D.B."},{"name":"Frisch T."},{"name":"Kaissis G."},{"name":"List M."},{"name":"Matschinske J."},{"name":"Nasirigerdeh R."},{"name":"Ruckert D."},{"name":"Spath J."},{"name":"Tieri P."},{"name":"Torkzadehmahani R."},{"name":"Wenke N.K."},{"name":"Zolotareva O."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Flimma: a federated and privacy-aware tool for differential gene expression analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC8670124","pmid":"34906207"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data security","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3263"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Microarray experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Flimma","home":"https://bio.tools/flimma","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Flimma is a federated privacy-aware version of state-of-the art differential expression analysis method limma voom.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:flimma/web/exbio.wzw.tum.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":16,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2023"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":5,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1186/s13059-021-02553-2","pmcid":"PMC8670124","pmid":"34906207","ref_count":75,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2001"},{"count":1,